From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:01:04 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: fold in two review findings

Neither changes behaviour today; both remove a trap for the next editor.

cbm_dp_port_alloc()'s field contract still promised
"data->deq_port = (u32)port_id + 5" and a "per-port DMA2TX handle". Both
are false for the WAN port, which resolves to dequeue port 19 on DMA1TX,
and this is the same class of stale comment the series has already been
through once -- missed here because the contract sits in the kerneldoc of
the very function whose body changed. State that the number is resolved
rather than computed, and name the WAN exception.

INIT_DELAYED_WORK moved inside the is_gswl branch when the MDIO driver
became per-instance, so a GSW-R priv now carries a delayed_work that was
never initialised. Harmless as it stands -- the driver has no .remove and
devm teardown never touches the struct -- but the obvious .remove would
add cancel_delayed_work_sync() for both buses and find it. Initialise
unconditionally and gate only the schedule, which is what the instance
check was ever about.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/switch-api/mdio_xrx500.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/switch-api/mdio_xrx500.c
index a0b208e6f498..15d798ad177c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/switch-api/mdio_xrx500.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/switch-api/mdio_xrx500.c
@@ -589,12 +589,10 @@ static int ltq_gswip_mdio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * GSW_HW_Init sequence. It runs from a work function because it must
 	 * not run from the MDIO bus callbacks it re-initialises.
 	 */
-	if (priv->is_gswl) {
-		INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&priv->gsw_reinit_work,
-				  ltq_gswip_gsw_reinit_work);
+	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&priv->gsw_reinit_work, ltq_gswip_gsw_reinit_work);
+	if (priv->is_gswl)
 		schedule_delayed_work(&priv->gsw_reinit_work,
 				      msecs_to_jiffies(LTQ_GSWIP_GSW_REINIT_DELAY_MS));
-	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
